        <div class="tab-content active" id="tab-assessment" data-main="vulns" data-sub="assessment">
            <div class="info">
                Select the <strong>locations</strong> to assess via the floating panel on the right. The table shows all findings of the
                selected locations; a rating you save applies to <strong>every selected location</strong> in which the finding occurs
                (no duplicate work per location). Ratings are stored per location and a non-empty comment is required for a rating.
                <strong>False positives</strong> are excluded from the vulnerability counts and need no comment.
                <br><br>
                Opening this page (and <em>Apply</em> in the location panel) reads the <strong>stored</strong> result - no device is
                touched, so it is instant. <strong>Scan &amp; Review</strong> is the only thing that queries the devices; while it runs
                the server stays usable (other tabs and the rest of MeshCentral keep answering), and a second panel that presses the
                button joins the running scan instead of starting another one. Automatic scans keep updating the stored result on their
                own schedule (Settings tab).
            </div>
            <div class="controls">
                <button id="scanBtn">Scan &amp; Review</button>
                <button id="locationToggle" class="location-toggle">Locations (<span id="locCountTxt">all</span>)</button>
                <span id="scanStatus"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="filter-row">
                <input type="text" id="filterText" class="filter-input" placeholder="Filter by CVE, software, device, location...">
                <select id="filterSeverity" class="filter-select">
                    <option value="">All Severities</option>
                    <option value="CRITICAL">Critical</option>
                    <option value="HIGH">High</option>
                    <option value="MEDIUM">Medium</option>
                    <option value="LOW">Low</option>
                    <option value="UNKNOWN">Unknown</option>
                    <option value="false positive">False Positive</option>
                </select>
                <select id="filterStatus" class="filter-select">
                    <option value="">All Statuses</option>
                    <option value="CVE">CVE</option>
                    <option value="false positive">False Positive</option>
                    <option value="rated">Rated</option>
                    <option value="unrated">Unrated</option>
                </select>
            </div>

            <div id="msg"></div>
            <div class="table-container" id="results"></div>
        </div>
